# Plaintext athlete data never belongs in this repo. These are minors and the
# published site is public regardless of repo visibility. One roster file does get
# committed: public/team.dat, which is scrambled first names and an initial, and
# no full name in the clear. See DESIGN.md.
roster*.csv
roster*.txt
roster*.json
/rosters/
*-splits.csv
# Meet results before they are scrambled. The tool reads full names out of here
# and ships public/*.dat holding first names and an initial. Same rule as the
# roster: the readable copy stays out of the repo.
/meets/
*-times.txt
jlmann-*.csv
# Working notes from reconciling a meet by hand. They quote real rows while the
# work is going on, which means full names next to times, so the whole directory
# stays out. A document meant for the repo goes at the top level next to
# DESIGN.md, where nothing is hiding it.
/docs/

# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
